  "review_findings": [
    "Current abstract and Introduction state P4 exclusion and full matching/triangle sign classification; P4 is not retained as an unresolved local positive sign type.",
    "Old three-high path proofs are not active. Stable mh18 and sm14 labels are preserved, and their proofs now invoke fh25 all-signs/matching without circular dependence.",
    "All-pair-product-strictly-positive assumption is retained. Two low rays with zero pair product are explicitly outside the unified theorem.",
    "Raw integer rows/pairs, positive weights where required, integer clutching, nonnegative node budget and opposite D remain explicit in G514 results.",
    "G514 five-node exclusion and aligned central matching are stated as structural reductions, not as exclusion of G514 itself.",
    "G516 general two-pattern unit-edge constraints are explicitly separated from G514-only five-node exclusion. G517 has no unit branch.",
    "Fixed-input finite reconstruction statements distinguish finite s or b input from uniform bounds or global nonexistence; endpoint s<=400 check is expressly bounded.",
    "Degenerate fixed-b reconstruction applies to x>=1; x=0 retains fixed-s route. Divisor denominators are positive and original rows/pairs/signs/D/weights are checked before recognizing a model.",
    "Remaining P4 strings in prime-support modules concern K1-join-P4 graph combinatorics, not a positive four-ray local sign candidate.",
    "Current literature discussion separates prior geometric existence, principal-minor, cycle-gain, Z-matrix and frieze theory from new integer gluing claims."
  ],
